# Disclosure phrasing. Substring match against the normalised transcript.
#
# EVERY LINE IN THIS FILE ROUTES A STUDENT TO A TEACHER. A false positive costs
# a real and awkward conversation, so the bar for adding one is high and the
# entries are phrases, never single words that could stand alone innocently.
# The README says to draft this with the school's wellbeing team, and that
# still holds: this file is a starting point for that conversation, not a
# substitute for it.
#
# What is deliberately NOT here, and why:
#   "i hate my life", "odio la mia vita", "sono depresso", "kill me"
#       - hyperbole is the register teenagers actually speak in, and a tool
#         that stops the exam every time someone says their life is terrible
#         will be switched off within a week, which protects nobody.
#   "morire", "die", "sterben" on their own
#       - a student whose grandfather died is describing their family, which is
#         exactly what the exam asked them to do.
#   anything built on "live" / "leben"
#       - "I don't want to live here any more" and "ich will nicht mehr hier
#         wohnen" are answers to "where do you live", which is a set topic.
#         The unambiguous phrasings below cover the same disclosure.
#
#
# A leading "!" marks an entry NON-ADJUDICABLE: the semantic reasoning pass
# (docs/compliance/compliant-flow.md, and sim/safety/adjudicator.hpp) may not
# reduce a verdict this phrase produced, whatever a model concludes about the
# context. The marker is stripped before matching, so it changes nothing about
# WHAT the entry matches - only what may afterwards be done about it.
#
# The rule for applying it: mark a phrase when you cannot construct a sentence
# in which a student says it and means something else. "voglio morire" is
# marked; "hits me" and "es beenden" are not, because "the song hits me" and
# "das Spiel beenden" exist.
#
# The asymmetry that decides the rest of the list: under-detecting a suicide
# disclosure and over-detecting one are not comparable errors, so where a
# phrase is unambiguous it is in even if it is rare.

# --- English: suicide ---------------------------------------------------------
!kill myself
!killing myself
i want to kill
!end my life
!ending my life
!take my own life
!taking my own life
end it all
!suicide
!suicidal
!commit suicide
want to die
wanna die
!i want to die
!i wish i was dead
!i wish i were dead
better off dead
!no reason to live
!nothing to live for
dont want to be here anymore
do not want to be here anymore
want to disappear
better off without me
nobody would miss me
no one would miss me
going to end it

# --- English: self-harm -------------------------------------------------------
hurt myself
hurting myself
!harm myself
!self harm
!cut myself
!cutting myself
cuts on my
burn myself

# --- English: abuse disclosure ------------------------------------------------
# Short and unambiguous only. "hurts me" is absent on purpose: a toothache
# hurts too.
hits me
beats me
hit me at home
being abused
touches me
touched me inappropriately
im scared to go home
i am scared to go home
scared of my dad
scared of my mum

# --- German: suicide ----------------------------------------------------------
!mich umbringen
!mich toten
!selbstmord
!suizid
!suizidal
!ich will sterben
!ich mochte sterben
will nicht mehr da sein
nicht mehr da sein wollen
es beenden
schluss machen mit allem
kein grund mehr
besser ohne mich
niemand wurde mich vermissen

# --- German: self-harm --------------------------------------------------------
mich verletzen
!mich ritzen
!ich ritze mich
mir wehtun
mich schneiden

# --- German: abuse disclosure -------------------------------------------------
schlagt mich
schlagen mich
hat mich geschlagen
angst nach hause
angst vor meinem vater
angst vor meiner mutter
fasst mich an
